  "fix_explanation": "This is a binary-compatibility failure, not a server misconfiguration. Options: (1) obtain a fancybattery build compiled for NeoForge 1.21.1; (2) if you own the source, rebuild against the 1.21.1 MDK and fix any compile errors (Item subclasses now typically register via DeferredRegister and accept Item.Properties); do NOT attempt runtime bytecode patching.",
  "code_patch": "// rebuild target (NeoForge 1.21.1 MDK):\npublic BatteryItem(Properties props) { super(props); }\n// neoforge.mods.toml dependency:\nversionRange = \"[1.21.1]\""
}

{
  "root_cause": "The mod constructor reads DeferredHolder.get() during the CONSTRUCT phase, but registry entries only become available after registry events finish (new registry event system - no 'RegistryEvent.Register' phase gating). Accessing the holder before entries are bound throws 'Registry Object not present'.",
